        "summary": "The Strait of Hormuz remains under severe operational stress. A single source, aninews.in, reports a commercial tanker struck by a drone in the strait, with UKMTO issuing a navigation advisory; the incident is not independently confirmed and no further details have been corroborated. Separately, UAE authorities have condemned what they describe as an Iranian attack on ADNOC vessels as an act of piracy, per news.webindia123.com, a claim that is also unverified and single-sourced. Iranian state media asserts that no commercial vessel can safely transit the strait without Iranian authorization, a claim originating with Mehr News and repeated through state channels; US officials have disputed this characterization. PortWatch's most recent published figure shows 1 transit recorded on 2026-08-09, against a pre-crisis baseline of 73 per day; port arrivals across Hormuz-area ports on both the Persian Gulf and Gulf of Oman sides totaled 549 in the most recent 24 hours, a distinct methodology from PortWatch data. At 11:53 UTC, 330 vessels were holding position away from berth and Brent was trading at $87.02, down 0.36% over 24 hours. The Crisis Pressure composite remains in the extreme band, driven primarily by physical transit deviation, while the Escalation Forecast sits in the elevated band, with Polymarket escalation contracts as the top contributor; the divergence between these two indices signals that current disruption is severe even as forward market pricing of further escalation has not moved higher.",
